[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mlocalStorage (Rec.)[39m
     [38;5;246mSynchronous, trivial, survives reload — which is what makes the catch-up pass demonstrable. Fine at this data size.
[39m  [38;5;246m2.[39m IndexedDB
     [38;5;246mAsync, scales further, survives more. Real API overhead for a to-do list that will never hold enough rows to need [39m
     [38;5;246mit.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m In-memory only
     [38;5;246mNo persistence. Simplest, but kills the catch-up-on-load feature entirely — the main value we just designed for.[39m
